WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.939
Gain multiplies each sample by a number. Greater than one amplifies; between zero and one attenuates.

2
00:00:06.596 --> 00:00:12.174
Inverting the polarity means multiplying by minus one: the curve is mirrored across the horizontal axis.

3
00:00:12.873 --> 00:00:18.843
Two signals are added sample by sample: the result at each instant is the sum of both values.

4
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:31.191
A delay shifts the signal in time. One millisecond at 48,000 samples per second is 48 samples: each sample comes out 48 positions later.
